# One line per WhatsApp account. Copy this file to instances.conf and edit it.
#
# instances.conf is gitignored, because it contains your phone numbers.
#
#   name       port   number          description
#
# name         Short label you choose: personal, work, us, brasil. It becomes
#              the store directory (store-<name>) and the server name Claude
#              sees (whatsapp-<name>), so pick something you'd recognise in a
#              list.
#
# port         Any free port. Each account needs its own.
#
# number       The phone number this account must be linked to, digits only,
#              with country code. The bridge prints the number that actually
#              scanned the QR code and refuses to start if it is not this one,
#              so a label can never quietly point at the wrong account.
#              Use "-" to skip the check.
#
# description  Free text, runs to the end of the line. Claude is told this, so
#              it knows which account to use. "Work number, colleagues and
#              clients" is far more useful to it than "work".

personal   8080   15555550134     Personal US number, family and friends
work       8081   5511999998888   Work Brazil number, colleagues and clients
